@startuml deployment
!include ../style.iuml
title Track Controller (HW) — Deployment

node "Host PC\nWindows 11, one machine, no network" as PC {
  artifact "TrackOverflow.exe\n(PyInstaller bundle)" as Exe
  node "Central harness process" as HP {
    component "Central Harness\nshared clock, edge mappings,\nevent log (CSV)" as Harness
  }
  node "Track Ctrl HW host process" as TP {
    component "Track Controller window\n(PySide6 / QML)" as Win
    component "RemoteTrackController\n+ PiSerialLink" as Remote <<planned>>
    component "HarnessEndpoint" as EP <<planned>>
  }
  node "Other module processes" as Others {
    component "CTC Office" as CTC
    component "Track Model" as TM
    component "Train Model" as TrM
    component "Track Ctrl SW (Green)" as TCSW
    component "Train Ctrl SW / HW host" as TrC
  }
  folder "Wayside data (host disk)" as Data {
    file "red_wayside_N.json\nwayside databases" as DB
    file "red_wayside_N.plc\nPLC programs" as PLC
  }
}

node "Raspberry Pi 5\nRaspberry Pi OS, Python 3" as Pi {
  component "PiLinkServer\nUSB gadget serial /dev/ttyGS0" as PiLink <<planned>>
  component "HwTrackController\nWayside ×N (Red Line)\nPLC engine: channels A, B\n+ vital block" as Core
}

node "Raspberry Pi\n(Train Ctrl HW)" as Pi2

Exe ..> HP : starts
HP --> TP : spawns
HP --> Others : spawns
Harness <--> EP : newline JSON\nrequest ID + tick (D005)
Harness <--> Others : newline JSON
EP --> Remote
Win --> Remote
Win ..> DB : Load database
Win ..> PLC : New PLC
Remote <--> PiLink : USB 2.0, CDC-ACM (COM port)\nnewline JSON (D027)
PiLink --> Core
TrC <--> Pi2 : USB serial

note bottom of Pi
  Power: the Pi 5's USB-C port is both its data link and its
  power input. A PC port may not supply enough for a Pi 5
  (5 V at 3 A minimum, 5 A recommended). Open item: a separate
  5 V supply (GPIO header or a data/power splitter).
end note
note right of TP
  The Track Ctrl HW test UI is a debug tool only:
  not packaged, never started by the harness.
end note
@enduml
